---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant WS as Workstation<br/>Gi1/0/1 · VLAN 10
    participant L1 as Leaf1<br/>Lo0 172.30.255.1
    participant BS as Border-Spine<br/>Lo0 172.30.255.3
    participant SD as SD-WAN edge<br/>AS 65534
    participant DH as DHCP / DNS / NTP<br/>198.18.5.102

    rect rgb(234, 244, 251)
    Note over WS,L1: Inside tenant VRF "Main"
    WS->>L1: DHCPDISCOVER (broadcast on VLAN 10)
    end

    Note over L1: Relay rewrites the packet:<br/>giaddr = 10.10.255.1 (SVI in VRF Main)<br/>Option 82 sub-opt 151 = VPN-ID "Main"<br/>source = Loopback0 (global table)<br/>destination looked up in the GLOBAL RIB

    rect rgb(234, 250, 241)
    Note over L1,DH: Outside every VRF — global routing table
    L1->>BS: Unicast relay over the OSPF underlay
    BS->>SD: Global-table eBGP path (neighbor 192.168.255.6)
    SD->>DH: Forwarded to the shared-services server
    Note over SD,DH: Reads Option 82 VPN-ID and giaddr,<br/>selects the scope for VRF Main / 10.10.255.0/24
    DH-->>SD: DHCPOFFER addressed to 172.30.255.1
    SD-->>BS: Return path: 172.30.255.1/32 is advertised<br/>to SD-WAN by the Border-Spine
    BS-->>L1: Unicast back to Loopback0
    end

    rect rgb(234, 244, 251)
    L1->>WS: DHCPOFFER relayed back into VLAN 10 / VRF Main
    Note over WS,L1: REQUEST / ACK repeat the same round trip
    end

    Note over WS,BS: Workstation now holds 10.10.255.x in VRF Main<br/>— no fusion router and no route leaking involved
